{"id":"sixth-street-viaduct","name":"Sixth Street Viaduct","qid":"Q123139315","country":"United States","locality":"Los Angeles","lat":"34.03836","lon":"-118.22692","built":"2022","year":2022,"year_text":"2022","century":"21st century","era":"20th century and later","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, official opening","style":"","heritage":"","type":"road bridge; viaduct","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixth_Street_Viaduct","text":"The Sixth Street Viaduct, also known as the Sixth Street Bridge, is a viaduct bridge that connects 6th Street in the Arts District in Downtown Los Angeles with Whittier Boulevard in the Boyle Heights neighborhood. The Sixth Street Viaduct spans the Los Angeles River, the Santa Ana Freeway (US 101), and the Golden State Freeway (I-5), as well as Metrolink (Orange County and 91/Perris Valley lines), Amtrak (Pacific Surfliner and Southwest Chief), and Union Pacific (along with Metrolink's Riverside Line) railroad tracks and several local streets. The first incarnation, which opened in 1932 and demolished in 2016, was replaced with the second incarnation in 2022.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixth_Street_Viaduct","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-938dd185f0d2","w":1200,"h":724,"title":"6th Street Bridge, Los Angeles Sunscape 3.jpg","o":"gh-938dd185f0d2.jpg","credit":{"text":"Downtowngal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:6th_Street_Bridge%2C_Los_Angeles_Sunscape_3.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"la-noire--6th-street-viaduct","game":"la-noire","name":"6th Street Viaduct","verified":false,"text":"The is a landmark in L.A. Noire. It is located on 6th Street above the Los Angeles River.","text_source":"https://lanoire.fandom.com/wiki/6th_Street_Viaduct","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-21d5c500d720","w":693,"h":565,"o":"gh-21d5c500d720.webp","credit":{"text":"Sc